Repair the complete source below. Export exactly `{ runConcurrentInOrder }` with `module.exports`.

`runConcurrentInOrder(tasks)` accepts an array of zero-argument functions. It must invoke every task without waiting for earlier promises to settle, assimilate synchronous values and promises, and return a promise whose values are in task input order regardless of completion order. An empty array resolves to `[]`, and any thrown error or rejection rejects the returned promise. A non-array or non-function element must throw `TypeError` synchronously. The task array must not be mutated.

Return a corrected complete source file.

```javascript
'use strict';

function runConcurrentInOrder(tasks) {
  if (!Array.isArray(tasks) || !tasks.every((task) => typeof task === 'function')) {
    throw new TypeError('tasks must be functions');
  }
  if (tasks.length === 0) return Promise.resolve([]);
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const results = [];
    let remaining = tasks.length;
    for (const task of tasks) {
      Promise.resolve().then(task).then((value) => {
        results.push(value);
        remaining -= 1;
        if (remaining === 0) resolve(results);
      }, reject);
    }
  });
}

module.exports = { runConcurrentInOrder };
```

